00:26:44.040 --> 00:26:47.440
We're on such good speaking terms since I continue to screw up which games.

00:26:47.520 --> 00:26:48.600
He's done so much, too.

00:26:49.800 --> 00:26:52.840
All right. So we've talked about the regular enemies here.

00:26:53.080 --> 00:26:54.020
We've talked about the bells.

00:26:54.180 --> 00:26:55.400
Do we want to talk about the boss fights?

00:26:55.680 --> 00:26:57.220
We should probably talk about the boss fights.

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:59.140
A.K.A. the best part of the game?

00:26:59.140 --> 00:27:05.960
Yes. That's the only good part of the game is the slightly inspired designs of these bosses.

00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:14.000
My favorite was probably the first, at least in the actual, like, visual of it.

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:18.360
It was just this giant-headed kid that, like, sneezes at you or something.

00:27:18.460 --> 00:27:20.000
That's V.O., too. Yeah.

00:27:20.280 --> 00:27:23.040
His actual name is Death Breath.

00:27:23.300 --> 00:27:24.440
Death Breath. Okay.

00:27:24.840 --> 00:27:30.460
Yeah. He has a gigantic head and he does three different ways of attacking you.

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:40.860
And it's, like, all of this work went in to making these bosses and not a single extra enemy could be made with these kind of, like, thoughts in mind, like, specific to their stages.

00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:45.060
Yeah. Where, like, they do similar things but on, like, a less threatening scale.

00:27:45.800 --> 00:27:48.080
I don't know. See, that's, like, confusing to me.

00:27:48.180 --> 00:27:51.860
It's, like, the bosses in this game are, I'm going to say it, pretty damn good.

00:27:51.860 --> 00:27:53.340
I had a lot of fun with most of them.

00:27:53.340 --> 00:28:08.960
I will say, though, and this is what I referred to earlier, that I don't understand, and I actually found it kind of frustrating, that you have to go and retrieve your sword whenever you attack a boss.

00:28:09.160 --> 00:28:11.280
Yes. I don't fault the bosses for that.

00:28:11.480 --> 00:28:15.600
No, no, no. The bosses had nothing to do with how bad you are at swinging a spinning sword.

00:28:16.440 --> 00:28:21.440
But it almost made me feel like I was not hitting them and this was the wrong way to fight.

00:28:21.520 --> 00:28:22.900
Sometimes I think you're not.

00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:25.240
I think it depends on the reaction from the boss.

00:28:25.440 --> 00:28:31.720
Yeah. It'll give you, like, an ugh graphic and he'll go backwards.

00:28:32.040 --> 00:28:37.380
Right. There's also, like, certain bosses that are just, like, they can only be hurt from a certain point or something.

00:28:37.540 --> 00:28:41.900
You know, like the witch who flies around the stage.

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:43.080
Oh, yeah, yeah. Third stage.

00:28:43.840 --> 00:28:47.560
She has a cape and if you attack from the cape side, it does no damage.

00:28:47.680 --> 00:28:57.980
Right. But why are you, you're sort of punishing the player for landing a hit by making him go and retrieve the goddamn sword.

00:28:58.020 --> 00:29:04.300
I know that it, like, makes it a little bit more of, like, a strategic thing because you want to hit him so that you can retrieve the sword quickly.

00:29:04.300 --> 00:29:06.140
But it happens every time.

00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:10.400
Yeah. And it takes most of the time, like, three to five hits to kill most of these guys.

00:29:10.940 --> 00:29:18.480
And I know it doesn't sound like a lot, but meanwhile, you have no weapon in your hand and you have to figure out a way to dodge the attacks that they're doing to you.

00:29:18.600 --> 00:29:19.900
And I get it. Like, there's some strategy.

00:29:19.900 --> 00:29:24.320
But it'd be nice if that only happened on, like, the very last hit before you killed the boss, you know?

00:29:24.380 --> 00:29:25.320
Like, so you do the hit.

00:29:25.340 --> 00:29:26.420
That would be a tension builder.

00:29:26.600 --> 00:29:29.400
Right. Exactly. Finally, now you don't have a weapon and you have to go retrieve it.

00:29:29.520 --> 00:29:32.620
That'd be cool. I'd be down for that even if it happened in every single boss.

00:29:32.920 --> 00:29:37.240
There's also this weird thing, though, where, you know, because your sword just, like, ricochets wherever.

00:29:37.540 --> 00:29:41.380
So one time my sword ricocheted all the way to, like, the top of the screen.

00:29:41.700 --> 00:29:43.080
And I'm like, how am I going to get that?

00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:44.680
So I go over to the edge of the screen and jump.

00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:49.600
And the game just teleports me to the sword, grabs it, and comes back down.

00:29:49.700 --> 00:29:51.080
And I'm like, oh, that's one way to solve it.

00:29:51.260 --> 00:29:54.660
At least they tested. That was where I was like, I was like, okay, that's kind of silly.

00:29:54.740 --> 00:29:55.640
But I was, like, at least impressed.

00:29:55.740 --> 00:29:58.620
But I was like, hey, at least they didn't just let it be game-breaking.

00:29:58.880 --> 00:30:00.240
Like, at least they knew that this was a problem.

00:30:00.240 --> 00:30:10.200
He doesn't have a sword anymore. But I'm still at a point, I think, in our nostalgia career where I'm, like, impressed by bosses having boss patterns.

00:30:10.760 --> 00:30:12.020
Because there's been so many that don't.

00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:14.100
Yeah. This isn't, we haven't had that many.

00:30:14.300 --> 00:30:15.320
No, we've had a couple.

00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:17.080
And I feel like I usually bring it up when we do.

00:30:17.300 --> 00:30:22.300
But when you think about what we just played before, Karate Kid, right, last week.

00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:26.120
And that game being essentially, oh, the boss is coming up?

00:30:26.220 --> 00:30:31.040
Well, some of these guys will just straight up jump off the platform if I just wait over here.

00:30:31.220 --> 00:30:32.820
You know, like, that level of dumb.

00:30:32.960 --> 00:30:35.980
It is really nice when you get to a boss like this.

00:30:36.020 --> 00:30:39.600
Because what I really like about these bosses is that they have multiple attacks.

00:30:39.600 --> 00:30:43.640
They have tells for when it's a good time to attack them.

00:30:44.120 --> 00:30:49.940
And they have, like, movement around the stage that makes sense to their particular characters.

00:30:50.200 --> 00:30:54.580
So it's not like they just hang on the right side of the screen and you have to charge at them.

00:30:54.700 --> 00:30:57.020
Yeah. There's a good time to attack all of these guys.

00:30:57.180 --> 00:30:59.160
I think that's what makes them such great bosses.

00:30:59.160 --> 00:31:02.180
They almost feel like early Mega Man bosses.

00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:03.740
Yeah. You know? I would say that.

00:31:03.940 --> 00:31:05.480
Yeah. Not nearly as inventive.

00:31:05.580 --> 00:31:07.140
No, exactly. Mega Man bosses are obviously awesome.

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:10.320
This is a primordial version of good boss design.

00:31:10.460 --> 00:31:11.500
Couldn't have said it better myself.

00:31:11.660 --> 00:31:16.440
But, yeah. Because I do think there were definitely flaws in the witch one that you said.

00:31:16.640 --> 00:31:18.760
Mm-hmm. Every time you hit this, I guess it's a witch.

00:31:18.840 --> 00:31:20.540
I don't even remember. I just remember something flying around.

00:31:20.800 --> 00:31:23.340
Every time you hit it, it splits into double of itself.

00:31:23.520 --> 00:31:25.760
Right. Into smaller versions of itself.

00:31:25.900 --> 00:31:27.140
And I was like, that's a cool concept.

00:31:27.900 --> 00:31:31.480
Until it's really, like, do you guys agree that was, like, the easiest boss by far?

00:31:31.480 --> 00:31:33.700
You just hit it six times and just hit them all.

00:31:33.900 --> 00:31:35.940
Like, they were, like, flying through me and not hitting me.

00:31:35.940 --> 00:31:37.960
It does so that it doesn't make it harder that there's more of them.

00:31:38.020 --> 00:31:41.080
It makes it easier to attack the ones that are directly in front of you.

00:31:41.180 --> 00:31:43.800
And also, now that I'm thinking about it, did that one, did you lose your sword in that

00:31:43.800 --> 00:31:45.880
one? I remember kind of just going and slashing away.

00:31:45.880 --> 00:31:46.720
Actually, you're right.

00:31:46.720 --> 00:31:48.980
I don't remember losing my sword in that boss battle.

00:31:49.340 --> 00:31:52.540
Which, the losing your sword didn't bother me too much anyways.

00:31:53.100 --> 00:31:54.720
Because I hadn't really thought about it too much.

00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:57.500
Well, I definitely, let me put it this way.

00:31:57.500 --> 00:32:01.380
I don't hate that it's in the game, but it's something that you notice.

00:32:01.880 --> 00:32:05.800
Right. That, like, every single time I hit one of these bosses, it goes flying.

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:08.480
And it does become a bigger deal in the final stage.

00:32:08.620 --> 00:32:11.520
Yes. But we'll talk about that when we get there.

00:32:11.600 --> 00:32:15.180
And again, it's just mixed messaging to the player.

00:32:15.660 --> 00:32:20.460
At least the first few times that you do it, it does not make sense that you've hit and

00:32:20.460 --> 00:32:24.840
you've lost your sword. It is not clear until you kind of, like, figure it all out.

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:30.020
But I will say that the, I think it was the fourth boss, which is like the centipede thing

00:32:30.020 --> 00:32:31.480
that's, like, going up and down.

00:32:31.580 --> 00:32:33.560
And you have to hit each, like, segment of it.

00:32:34.860 --> 00:32:39.260
That, I think, the gameplay, I mean, granted, there's other ways to make the gameplay more

00:32:39.260 --> 00:32:43.080
challenging. But I think that losing your sword every time helped the gameplay.

00:32:43.200 --> 00:32:46.480
Because otherwise, I feel like it would have been very easy to just kill him all at once.

00:32:46.780 --> 00:32:53.300
That's true. And then one other thing I want to say about the losing your sword is that the, I guess

00:32:53.300 --> 00:32:57.540
it's the fifth boss, then, is like the suit of armor holding, like, a spear above his

00:32:57.540 --> 00:32:58.680
head? Stage six.

00:32:58.980 --> 00:33:02.440
Six. Five is the big baldy who screams at you.

00:33:02.640 --> 00:33:03.840
Oh, fool, right?

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:05.200
Yeah. He calls you a fool.

00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:09.020
Yeah. He screams at you and you have to dodge his screams and commands.

00:33:09.240 --> 00:33:10.580
I liked that boss fight.

00:33:10.680 --> 00:33:14.400
But more of what I really liked about that stage were those giant Buddha statues.

00:33:14.760 --> 00:33:17.380
Oh, yeah. The bits in this game are pretty mediocre for the most part.

00:33:17.540 --> 00:33:18.700
But then I'm like, yeah, that's a pretty detailed Buddha.

00:33:18.700 --> 00:33:22.880
They saved all of their art department for these, like, two Buddha statues in this one

00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:26.760
stage. I mean, if you're going to do it for something, might as well do it for something that's, like,

00:33:26.840 --> 00:33:28.000
respectful, I guess, at least.

00:33:28.440 --> 00:33:29.460
I guess so.

00:33:31.020 --> 00:33:36.540
But for, so then for the fouling boss, well, first, I do want to mention that that guy who

00:33:36.540 --> 00:33:42.940
yells fool at you, a cloud of what he's saying appears above, above you, and it says fool.

00:33:42.940 --> 00:33:47.940
And then this cloud of fool drops a bunch of little, like, letters, like, F-O-O-Ls on

00:33:47.940 --> 00:33:49.000
you. It's cute. Yeah.

00:33:49.140 --> 00:33:51.680
That's what I kind of meant when I meant there's, like, some charm to this game.

00:33:51.760 --> 00:33:57.820
Yeah. But what did you guys think of that suit of armor guy holding the spear?

00:33:57.820 --> 00:33:59.640
I didn't know what I was doing wrong.

00:34:00.280 --> 00:34:04.540
Yeah. Hated it because I couldn't tell, like, what I was doing.

00:34:04.540 --> 00:34:08.480
And eventually what I just came up with, I'm not even sure if this is the strategy, but

00:34:08.480 --> 00:34:13.160
I just made it so that he got as close to me as possible on the left side of the screen

00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:15.100
because he's in guard mode the entire time.

00:34:15.340 --> 00:34:19.020
I'd attack him, be able to pick up my sword right away because it would just deflect right

00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:22.700
to the end of the screen, and attack him again before he could go back into his guard

00:34:22.700 --> 00:34:27.200
stance. And when you have to cheese the game, I mean, like, okay, so we're talking about good boss

00:34:27.200 --> 00:34:29.000
design. This was the dud.

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:34.520
So I gathered by the end, I thought that you had to hit him on the jump and hit him

00:34:34.520 --> 00:34:37.020
on top of the head, which was working for me.

00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:38.800
Really? Yeah. I could be wrong.

00:34:38.920 --> 00:34:40.560
Maybe there's something else at play there.

00:34:40.740 --> 00:34:45.400
But the thing is, before I figured this out, I actually thought this was the coolest boss

00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:47.280
design until I realized what it really was.

00:34:47.440 --> 00:34:52.380
Because I thought what you're supposed to do, which is not true, is when you hit this boss,

00:34:52.820 --> 00:34:57.520
your sword falls out and goes to the other end of the screen, but his spear also falls

00:34:57.520 --> 00:34:59.480
out and goes to the opposite end of the screen is your sword.

00:34:59.660 --> 00:35:00.920
Not as far away, though.

00:35:01.220 --> 00:35:06.120
Not as far away, but he scuttles back to get his spear while you have to run back at your

00:35:06.120 --> 00:35:11.360
sword. And I thought the goal was to get him off of his end of the screen, but it would be

00:35:11.360 --> 00:35:15.520
like a constant race to get to your sword and get back to him to keep knocking him back.

00:35:15.600 --> 00:35:18.360
And I got him really close to the off, but I don't think it's possible.

00:35:18.540 --> 00:35:20.460
Right. No, apparently that is the idea.

00:35:20.940 --> 00:35:24.940
Oh. No, like that, yeah, essentially you want to get to a point where you'll be able to retrieve

00:35:24.940 --> 00:35:26.140
your sword faster than he is.

00:35:26.140 --> 00:35:28.000
Oh, yes. Right. But that's not what I thought it was.

00:35:28.140 --> 00:35:31.280
I'm just saying like it doesn't matter anyway because at the end of the day, the only way

00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:33.260
to really have that work is to cheese it.

00:35:33.340 --> 00:35:35.080
And I don't think that that's...

00:35:35.080 --> 00:35:35.880
Right. Fun.

00:35:36.120 --> 00:35:41.320
That's fun, right. This one, I would say like I thought I was doing damage to him for a while and then I

00:35:41.320 --> 00:35:44.400
realized like there's no way this boss takes like 13 hits to kill.

00:35:44.540 --> 00:35:46.140
And I realized I just wasn't doing anything yet.

00:35:46.260 --> 00:35:47.520
I haven't even started fighting him.

00:35:47.820 --> 00:35:53.380
Yeah. If they had gotten it to work that way, though, where you have to knock, you have to get him off

00:35:53.380 --> 00:35:57.160
of his end of the screen while having to go continuously retrieve your sword.

00:35:57.380 --> 00:36:01.960
I think that would have been a good like, not finale, but a good payoff to the whole losing

00:36:01.960 --> 00:36:03.480
your sword gameplay mechanic.

00:36:03.680 --> 00:36:06.100
Yeah. It's like, oh, this is like where I put what I learned to the test.

00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:07.420
Yeah. But not so.

00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:11.100
Well, I learned about dropping my sword and getting it.

00:36:11.480 --> 00:36:13.740
It would have been... Hey, that's a good motif, though.

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:14.920
I would have liked that.

00:36:15.140 --> 00:36:17.520
You know? Keep it back up.

00:36:17.700 --> 00:36:22.060
Yeah. Before we go to the final stage, stage seven, I'd like to talk about the secret areas.

00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:24.400
Did you guys experience any of those?

00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:26.200
Nope. I'm on my own.

00:36:26.460 --> 00:36:30.000
I went to one of them only after I saw it happen in a Let's Player.

00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:31.300
And I'm trying to remember what it was.

00:36:31.340 --> 00:36:33.960
I had to hit certain columns or something.

00:36:34.080 --> 00:36:35.580
I honestly don't even really remember.

00:36:35.580 --> 00:36:42.860
My favorite one that I saw was, I think you have to accidentally die by falling into water.

00:36:42.880 --> 00:36:46.500
And then you get eaten by like a sea monster of sorts.

00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:48.040
And then you were just in his stomach.

00:36:48.360 --> 00:36:49.700
Yes. That's the best one.

00:36:49.800 --> 00:36:51.140
I was actually just about to mention that.

00:36:51.260 --> 00:36:55.700
Yes. You fall into the space between the island and the fish.

00:36:55.700 --> 00:36:58.440
And then you get transported into the belly of the fish.

00:36:58.600 --> 00:37:00.960
That was the secret area I was going to mention because it's the most interesting.

00:37:01.160 --> 00:37:03.020
Because you actually see like the skeleton.

00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:05.180
What would you call it?

00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:07.040
Of the fish.

00:37:07.340 --> 00:37:09.000
No, no, no. But it's not like necessarily the skeleton.

00:37:09.160 --> 00:37:10.160
It's the spine. Yeah, the spine.

00:37:10.340 --> 00:37:16.200
Yeah. Sorry. And it's just weird that they relegated their most interesting map design with like context

00:37:16.200 --> 00:37:21.020
and like not just random islands that you have to jump over to these bonus areas.

00:37:21.160 --> 00:37:23.400
Because even like I guess you climb a tree.

00:37:23.780 --> 00:37:27.960
Yeah. And you climb a tree, which is just like not something I would have even done in the game.

00:37:28.060 --> 00:37:30.500
I never really thought about like, oh, scale the trees.

00:37:30.500 --> 00:37:34.280
Like, you know, like when a vine pops up in Super Mario, it's like, yeah, scale that vine.

00:37:34.580 --> 00:37:38.680
Yeah. Like when a tree is just in the game, I'm not thinking like, oh, yeah, Kid Nicky is known

00:37:38.680 --> 00:37:39.720
for climbing trees.

00:37:40.860 --> 00:37:43.840
Also, there's some other weird things like in that same stage.

00:37:44.260 --> 00:37:49.360
If you just go to the at the very beginning of the stage, just go to the very left of the

00:37:49.360 --> 00:37:54.960
screen and squat for several seconds, you'll just be transported to a tunnel with a bunch

00:37:54.960 --> 00:37:55.880
of eggs in them.

00:37:56.100 --> 00:38:01.840
And then there's like a not like a dinosaur, but like some kind of green worm thingy that

00:38:01.840 --> 00:38:02.720
looks like a dinosaur.

00:38:02.960 --> 00:38:03.960
They're like, Jason, after you.

00:38:04.020 --> 00:38:06.180
And I'm like, I don't remember seeing him anywhere else in the game.

00:38:06.180 --> 00:38:08.380
So like, why is he also only in this secret area?

00:38:08.600 --> 00:38:10.660
Yeah. There's just so many things that they put into the secret area.

00:38:10.660 --> 00:38:16.040
Like even in the Buddha stage where there's like four different temples that you can go

00:38:16.040 --> 00:38:20.980
to as secret areas that have like cool power ups and other neat things to pick up.

00:38:21.040 --> 00:38:23.820
Maybe we're just not paying good enough attention.

00:38:24.260 --> 00:38:29.120
I don't know. I feel like they wouldn't have put this much effort into these areas if they didn't think

00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:30.200
that people could find them.

00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:31.760
Okay. Well, how about this one?

00:38:31.880 --> 00:38:34.880
Okay. This one you can only get to in the Famicom version.

00:38:35.300 --> 00:38:37.720
Wow. They expected us to buy the Famicom version?

00:38:37.720 --> 00:38:42.380
In this one, you have to, you go on to the giant Buddha statue that we all love so much

00:38:42.380 --> 00:38:43.280
that we thought was interesting.

00:38:43.500 --> 00:38:46.660
And you squat in the middle of its lap.

00:38:46.980 --> 00:38:51.220
And then you yell into the microphone that's in the Famicom controller.

00:38:51.860 --> 00:38:58.780
And then that will transport you to the bonus area where you'll get like some extra coins

00:38:58.780 --> 00:39:01.480
and princess dolls and extra lives.

00:39:01.680 --> 00:39:03.200
And show the trailer for Silent Hills.

00:39:03.840 --> 00:39:08.500
Yeah. That's really funny that they would have that in 1987.

00:39:09.560 --> 00:39:16.480
Suspicious. So I think that like the verdict I'm getting from this is that the secret areas are awesome

00:39:16.480 --> 00:39:17.880
and very thoughtful.

00:39:18.560 --> 00:39:23.620
But like, geez, put them in like a manual or something.

00:39:23.860 --> 00:39:25.880
Like give us some hints on how to find these things.

00:39:25.880 --> 00:39:30.560
It's almost like they planned on selling you a DLC strategy guide.

00:39:30.940 --> 00:39:33.860
You know, like where you'd be able to download the content.

00:39:34.060 --> 00:39:35.440
Yeah. I knew what you meant.

00:39:36.600 --> 00:39:38.440
It's more of a microtransaction, right?

00:39:38.640 --> 00:39:39.440
In that regard.

00:39:39.460 --> 00:39:40.340
It was just a transaction.

00:39:40.400 --> 00:39:41.940
I think it's just buying a strategy guide.

00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:43.060
A macro transaction.

00:39:43.700 --> 00:39:45.600
Oh, capital.

00:39:45.600 --> 00:39:51.320
Capital. Even if they didn't have like a hint to get to it, like make it discoverable in the game.

00:39:51.520 --> 00:39:53.660
Like make it. I mean, I guess it hints within the game.

00:39:53.860 --> 00:39:56.960
