00:50:09.840 --> 00:50:12.300
My God. Related to pausing the game.

00:50:12.460 --> 00:50:14.660
Great. I love a good pause tangent.

00:50:14.660 --> 00:50:17.620
Because you know every couple episodes I like to put the pause in there.

00:50:18.160 --> 00:50:20.760
It's not really about the sound of pausing the game.

00:50:20.760 --> 00:50:26.900
It's about when you pause this game and when you unpause it, the music starts over.

00:50:27.600 --> 00:50:28.880
Did you guys notice it?

00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:29.860
I didn't. The music starts at the beginning.

00:50:30.180 --> 00:50:33.260
So every time you pause it, it starts with the intro music to the level again.

00:50:33.460 --> 00:50:38.300
I just figured that was a good little straight thought to add to the Joe's Pause Sounds archives.

00:50:38.300 --> 00:50:39.460
The compendium. Yes.

00:50:39.480 --> 00:50:40.540
Yeah, that's actually good to know.

00:50:40.660 --> 00:50:45.600
This is actually a controversy that's happening right now in Final Fantasy IX on Nintendo Switch and Steam.

00:50:45.600 --> 00:50:49.180
It's a game where every single time you're in the overworld, you hear the music.

00:50:49.320 --> 00:50:52.400
When you go to a boss fight and you come out of – not a boss fight.

00:50:52.460 --> 00:50:57.800
When you go to any kind of random encounter and you come back, it starts the song all over again from the beginning.

00:50:58.020 --> 00:51:01.820
So nobody's able to hear like two minutes into the track or whatever.

00:51:02.560 --> 00:51:07.820
And I'm like, you know, this is now – this is a problem that has been going on since 87.

00:51:07.840 --> 00:51:09.200
It's tearing the community apart.

00:51:09.840 --> 00:51:12.180
What's funny is it can't be that hard to fix.

00:51:12.400 --> 00:51:13.300
Why don't they just fix it?

00:51:13.320 --> 00:51:14.680
They fixed it for Final Fantasy VII.

00:51:14.940 --> 00:51:16.140
Yeah. Who knows?

00:51:16.220 --> 00:51:18.980
Maybe by the time this episode publishes, they'll have fixed it.

